<title>USA: Berkshire converts Salomon preferred.</title>
<headline>Berkshire converts Salomon preferred.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Units of Berkshire Hathaway Inc, the insurance company controlled by investor Warren Buffett, have converted 140,000 preferred shares in Salomon Inc into common shares, Berkshire Hathaway said in a Securities and Exchange Commission filing on Friday.</p>
<p>According to the filing, the units exercised their option to convert the preferred shares into common shares on October 29. Berkshire Hathaway and Buffett now hold the equivalent of a 17.8 percent stake in Salomon, consisting of 10,317,806 common shares and 420,000 preferred shares, the filing showed.</p>
<p>Berkshire Hathaway's plan to convert the preferred shares was announced by Salomon on September 12.</p>
